906,"# Hadith Translation

**Narrated to us al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth and others, one of them said: Narrated to us al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā, from Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid, from ʿIlbāʾ ibn Aḥmar, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:**

""We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and the time of the sacrifice (al-Aḍḥā) arrived. We shared in a cow among seven persons and in a camel among ten persons.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a *ḥasan gharīb* (good yet rare) hadith, and it is the ḥadīth of Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid.

---

**Note:** This hadith is found in *Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī* and pertains to the permissibility of sharing in sacrificial animals during the festival of Eid al-Aḍḥā, with up to seven participants sharing a cow or ten sharing a camel, based on the Companions' practice with the Prophet ﷺ."
